  "text": "World History — Bullet Points ASCII mindmap One liner frames for Mains WWI \"spark vs structures\": Sarajevo was the trigger; the alliance blocs + imperial competition were the fuel. WWII = \"Versailles' unfinished business\" + fascist ideological war (not just German territorial goals). Decolonisation diversity: \"Asia by statute (mostly), Africa by insurrection (often)\" — with India shifting model. Industrial Revolution's India link: raw cotton in, finished Manchester out (terms of trade reversal). Cold War end: not a single cause — military overreach + economic stagnation + legitimacy deficit + Eastern European agency. Date pattern drills 1905: Japan beats Russia (first Asian reversal of a European power). 1911: Chinese revolution (Sun Yat sen); 1949 PRC; 1971 UN seat. 1967: Six Day War; 1973 Yom Kippur → first oil shock; 1979 Iranian Revolution.",
