  "text": "World History — Revision Notes Fast recall sheet for Mains answers — cause effect chains, not dates. Industrial Revolution chain Agricultural revolution + empire revenue + property rights + coal/iron + banking → textile tech (Jenny 1764 → mule 1779 → Watt 1769) → factory system → urban labour class → imperial realignment (deindustrialising colonies) → second wave (steel/chemicals/electricity, 1870–1914) → Fordism/Taylorism → mass consumption states. Ideology quick table Liberalism: rights, limited govt (Locke, Mill) — revolutions of 1688/1776/1789. Socialism: exploitation critique (Owen, Fourier) → welfare states. Marxism Leninism: 1848 Manifesto → 1917 Bolshevik → planned economies. Fascism/Nazism: Mussolini (1922 march on Rome), Hitler (1933 enabling act). Keynes: 1936 General Theory → post war welfare settlements (Beveridge 1942). Colonisation → decolonisation Berlin 1884–85 scramble ",
