  "text": "Polity — Prelims PYQs Pattern faithful MCQs. Exact PYQ nature hedged; answers original. Q1. Which amendment substituted \"armed rebellion\" for \"internal disturbance\" in Article 352? (a) 42nd (b) 44th (c) 52nd (d) 73rd Model answer: (b). The 44th (1978) also restricted Art 356 abuse and shielded Arts 20–21. Q2. With reference to Money Bills: 1. The Speaker's certification is final. 2. Rajya Sabha can amend and return within 14 days. (a) 1 only (b) 2 only (c) Both (d) Neither Model answer: (a). RS can only recommend amendments within 14 days; LS may accept/reject. Q3. [PYQ pattern] The \"procedure established by law\" clause in Article 21 was borrowed from: (a) UK (b) USA (c) Japan (d) Ireland Model answer: (c). USA's phrase is \"due process of law\" — the standard PYQ distinction. Q4. Which DPSP directs equitable distribution of material resources? (a) Art 38 (b) Art 39(b) & 39(c) (c) Art 44 (",
